From 803a0e7c4ed77c7badf131e6e14878f1a49929bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Upstream Contributor <contributor@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:44:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add group-aware splits and a leakage check

output_split shuffles sample by sample, so the translations or paraphrases
of one item can land in both train and test, and a test score then measures
memorisation.

Add output_split_group (CuratorConfig and YAML), a metadata key whose value
keeps a group in one split. A group's split is a hash of its id and
output_split_seed, so an item keeps its split as the corpus grows, which a
shuffle can't do. Split sizes then only approximate the fractions. Without
the option, splitting is unchanged and tests pin it to the old shuffle.

Add curatorkit.splits. split_samples is now the one split path: Curator and
the CLI each had their own copy. leakage_report finds groups, exact prompts
and near-duplicate prompts in more than one split, and a grouped run warns
when it finds any. It compares prompts, not prompt plus answer, because one
prompt with two answers still leaks.

Language ID is not part of this change.
